message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "Orch-OR Visualizer: an interactive model of orchestrated objective reduction"
authors:
  - family-names: Seong
    given-names: John
    email: wonmor@yahoo.com
version: "1.0"
date-released: "2026-10-04"
url: "https://wonmor.github.io/orch-or/"
repository-code: "https://github.com/wonmor/OrchOR"
license: MIT
abstract: "An interactive teaching model of the Penrose–Hameroff Orch-OR theory: a 3D microtubule lattice in which tubulin superposition spreads by orchestration, accumulates gravitational self-energy, and undergoes objective reduction when the integral of E_G over time reaches ħ, calibrated to Hameroff and Penrose (2014), with a decoherence switch for the Tegmark and Hagan et al. estimates and a Diósi–Penrose calculator."
keywords: [Orch OR, consciousness, objective reduction, microtubules, simulation, physics education, iOS]
